After two ascension, with a valk and a samurai, I've decided next try a
non-melee character. I chose elven wizard. After 78 tries and early
YASD's I'm getting desparate. The deepest I've gotten was Dlvl 11,
however 48 times I've gotten killed on Dlvl 3 or earlier. The most
common causes of death are:

7 times by a small mimic (+1 giant mimic)
7 times by a dwarf (+1 dwarf lord)
4 times by a sewer rat
3 times by a gnome lord
... (+many obscure deaths, like killed by kickin a rock and killed by
sipping boiling water)

This is how I've done it so far:
I'll always try to raise my pet first, many times I've had large cat
when I got killed. I avoid leveling, even if I'm not going for
protection run. I'll take notes: what turn I prayed last, what levels
had store, what levels had vault, shop, fountains, sinks, where are
stairs to mine and where is Sokoban (if I get there). I'll try to be
careful, and try to survive the best I can (even though after so many
early deaths it sometimes is difficult to keep up the concentration).

Maybe 3/4 times I go first to mines, and most of those times I'll try
to reach to the mines while Exl lvl 1-3 (protection run). Most of the
very early deaths are a result of such attempt -- I find it very
difficult to stay alive at Exp: 1 in mines. I know that chaotic Elven
is difficult in the mines, but who wants to be a gnome, really? And
human is out of the question too, without infravision I'll die in dark
mines even sooner.

I also know that praying when your HP is below 5 might result God
raising your HP by few points, but that doesn't seem to be enough.
Those couple of times I've gotten to mines before me or my pet are
killed, and before my Exp lvl getting >3, I've been hugely unlucky with
either mine town having next to no stores (for example, only lighting
and delicatessen) so I don't have money, or had bones with angry pets
and/or difficult monster that take me before I can say: blueberrypie.

